#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:5
#: 067611895c334a9eb03cf85b08ce6bbd
msgid "QAUTOTUNE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:7
#: d30d1edebda84a8d90c4498ccb518afa
msgid "``DEPRECATED: still available in custom builds.`` Use :ref:`quicktune`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:9
#: 3f284b4273084973bc67192ef64e5510
msgid "Autotuning PIDs in QuadPlane is supported with this flight mode. This uses the same system as the AUTOTUNE mode for copter. It should allow you to improve the tune without having to manually adjust PIDs. It is not recommended to use QAUTOTUNE for Tailsitter pitch or yaw axis, or any axis which requires feed forward pid contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:12
#: 4fd0e6f37eeb4de9914371109aef807e
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:14
#: 780e39d458634af18f9ab8f6da161ef0
msgid "Set QAUTOTUNE mode (mode 22) on one of your mode switch positions. It may not show up as an available mode in your GCS, so you may need to set the ``FLTMODEn`` parameter in the full parameter list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:15
#: 425395edc01a408dbeb84503dca0fe99
msgid "Select which axes you want to tune with :ref:`Q_AUTOTUNE_AXES<Q_AUTOTUNE_AXES>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:18
#: 8bbdb1f7019243a69c03d9e85ca77055
msgid "Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:20
#: 88c151b31a3245de9591d373a101ecc4
msgid "QAUTOTUNE mode cannot be entered while disarmed, unlike many other QuadPlane modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:22
#: 48a02438701446db8ca9b4c51a08710b
msgid "As a QAUTOTUNE can take quite a long time (3 to 5 minutes per axis is common) you may wish to tune one axis at a time. Choose whether you want position hold support while tuning. If you enter QAUTOTUNE mode from QLOITER then it will use a loose position hold, preventing wind from carrying it away while tuning. If you start from QHOVER then it will not hold position, and you may need to reposition while tuning, but it will only do tuning (“twitching” to measure responses) while the sticks are centered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:24
#: b647e29ea5ed4c67b86fe212b3f1b74a
msgid "You may need to increase the deadzone (``RCx_DZ``) on your input channels or re-calibrate your RC channels to ensure it can start the tune. Once you start the tune it will “twitch” on the axis it is tuning. So if it is tuning roll, then it does small sharp roll movements to measure response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:26
#: 29af381bf4294a2393de37ce3e0faaaf
msgid "You can tell that QAUTOTUNE has finished when it stops twitching. You need to then land while staying in QAUTOTUNE mode and disarm without changing modes to save the tune. If you land in QAUTOTUNE and disarm after some axes have completed ,but the whole tune is not complete, then the PIDs for the axes that have completed will be saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:28
#: aa9d6471a2ee4b669963e45ce80b5808
msgid "You can reposition while tuning by moving your sticks. Once you re-center the sticks the tune will continue. If you change modes then the tune stops immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:30
#: 0d9e618b6ba445b3a9e34379d7eddbbe
msgid "You can read more about AutoTune for copters here: :ref:`autotune`. The autotune for quadplanes works the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qautotune-mode.rst:32
#: 3541ce708c8b42f09a92e26506fbb214
msgid "Like Copter, entering QAUTOTUNE from QLOITER will attempt a loose position hold."
msgstr ""
